`,a.jsxs(e.p,{children:["How much of an eager forward goes to the attention kernel that the backends compete on, and how much to the small operations between the matrix multiplications? A staff script, ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"scripts/staff/w04_compile_profile.py"}),", answers this on the same kind of H100. It reuses ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"measure_arm"}),", the FLOP count and the roofline of the gold ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"compare.py"})," unchanged. It times each arm on ",a.jsx("code",{children:Q.backend})," eager and under ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"torch.compile"}),". Its eager latencies agree with the gold points within ",o(h.eagerRerunDrift,1),". For ",a.jsx("code",{children:Q.arm})," it also records every GPU kernel with the PyTorch profiler and assigns each to a part of the model. A matrix multiplication is assigned by the shape of its weight. Any other kernel is assigned by the module that launched it when eager, and by the operations its generated name lists when compiled, because compilation fuses across module boundaries."]}),`
